From c106c0055b79c772437db32e41962489ce1e54ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nobody <nobody@localhost>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:11:29 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] tcg: add hand-off interface and guarded translation
 blocks

Add the interface an external x86 engine uses to take over TCG vCPUs:
TcgHandoffOps, EXCP_HANDOFF, and CF_HANDOFF_GUARD. No engine is
registered by this patch, so TCG behaviour is unchanged.

A guarded TB records the exact guest bytes it was translated from, so
that an engine's stores that bypass TCG's notdirty path cannot leave a
stale block in use. The recorded bytes live in extra space placed after
the TB by tcg_tb_alloc(), which now takes the number of extra bytes.
tb_gen_code() reports through *reused when it discards a translation
in favour of one already published.

Ported from the QEMU integration of Hybrid Hypervisor in Virtual Intel
Mac. Hybrid Hypervisor was invented by Sam Henri Gold (developer of
Light Touch, https://github.com/samhenrigold). Virtual Intel Mac is by
nfzerox.

Source commit: https://github.com/nfzerox/VirtualIntelMacOnAppleSilicon/commit/0c29f1f0fcaff59fdb6721f7ffa8b4a8c8decb65
Files, under Source/vendor/qemu/ at that commit:
  include/accel/tcg/handoff.h
  include/exec/tcg-handoff-code.h
  accel/tcg/translate-all.c
  accel/tcg/translator.c
  tcg/tcg.c
  include/exec/cpu-common.h
  include/exec/translation-block.h

Originally-by: Sam Henri Gold <49251320+samhenrigold@users.noreply.github.com>
Originally-by: nfzerox <nfzerox@protonmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
